Message from libsigrok-0.5.2:

On Linux, you may need to install udev rules for non-root access to
USB-based measurement devices. Example rules are installed at:

	${PREFIX}/share/examples/libsigrok/60-libsigrok.rules
	${PREFIX}/share/examples/libsigrok/61-libsigrok-plugdev.rules
	${PREFIX}/share/examples/libsigrok/61-libsigrok-uaccess.rules

Copy the ones appropriate for your setup to your system udev rules
directory (e.g. /etc/udev/rules.d/) and reload the rules with:

	udevadm control --reload-rules && udevadm trigger
